        <h2>About Oriana Haran, MD</h2>
        <p>
          Oriana Haran, MD, is a double fellowship-trained plastic and reconstructive surgeon, currently serving as an
          assistant
          professor in the Division of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery at The University of Texas Health Science
          Center at San
          Antonio. She is the only female plastic surgeon at UT Health San Antonio, uniquely positioned to offer her
          patients a
          blend of leading-edge expertise and compassionate, patient-centered care.
        </p>
        <p>
          Haran specializes in breast reconstruction, providing advanced options that include both implants and
          autologous tissue
          (using the patient’s own tissue, such as from the abdomen or inner thighs). She is proficient in advanced
          microsurgical
          techniques, including deep inferior epigastric perforator (DIEP), superficial inferior epigastric artery
          (SIEA), diagonal
          upper gracilis (DUG) and profunda artery perforator (PAP) flaps, which offer patients natural, long-lasting
          reconstruction
          results.
        </p>
        <p>
          She is also highly skilled in the prevention and treatment of breast cancer-related lymphedema, making her a
          trusted ally
          for women undergoing breast cancer treatment. She has a particular interest in addressing complex issues
          related to
          implant-based breast reconstruction, such as post-radiation capsular contracture and implant-associated
          anaplastic large
          cell lymphoma (ALCL), ensuring that her patients receive the safest and most effective care possible.
        </p>
        <p>
          Haran is an accomplished academic with a distinguished record of research and publications. Her international
          training and
          experience have equipped her to provide her patients with personalized care and innovative solutions.
          Passionate about
          empowering women, she offers comprehensive breast reconstruction options tailored to their individual needs
          and goals,
          ensuring improved patient outcomes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Haran is fluent in English, Spanish and Hebrew, allowing her to connect with diverse patients. Outside of
          work, she enjoys
          playing tennis, traveling and spending quality time with her daughter.
        </p>

